; A .skool with no absolute store in it, for the fixtures whose subject is the
; set of pages a .ctl publishes rather than the type of any one entry.
;
; `validate_ctl_publication.py` takes the .skool as a required argument - a
; linter that silently skips half its checks is worse than one that is not wired
; up - so `fixtures/outside-image.ctl` and `fixtures/fragmented-structure.ctl`
; are run against this one. It yields no write target, so MUTABLE reports nothing
; and each fixture is left proving its own kind alone.
@start
@org
; Program entry
@label=start
c$4002 XOR A             ;
 $4003 RET               ;
